1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:05,359
Axin uses a Next.js frontend, a modular Spring Boot backend, and a

2
00:00:05,359 --> 00:00:09,700
database. Here is how a request flows through the system.

3
00:00:10,150 --> 00:00:16,174
The frontend groups code by feature. React components handle journeys, maps, and

4
00:00:16,174 --> 00:00:22,198
operator tools. Shared shadcn components provide controls, while Leaflet displays routes and

5
00:00:22,198 --> 00:00:22,700
markers.

6
00:00:23,150 --> 00:00:29,425
Browser requests pass through a same-origin Next.js proxy to Spring Boot. The

7
00:00:29,425 --> 00:00:35,700
proxy restricts paths and applies timeouts. Live snapshots refresh every three seconds.

8
00:00:36,150 --> 00:00:42,404
Backend packages follow business features. Controllers handle requests, services coordinate operations, and

9
00:00:42,404 --> 00:00:48,658
policies calculate rules. Repositories handle database access, with some services also using

10
00:00:48,658 --> 00:00:49,700
JDBC directly.

11
00:00:50,150 --> 00:00:56,925
Flyway manages database migrations. The catalog loads from versioned open data. Reports,

12
00:00:56,925 --> 00:01:03,700
alerts, vehicles, and assignments persist. Transactions and idempotency help prevent duplicate writes.

13
00:01:04,150 --> 00:01:10,172
The journey engine checks nearby stops and directed route geometry. It prioritizes

14
00:01:10,172 --> 00:01:16,194
fewer boardings. Arrival estimates add walking, simulated waiting, riding, and transfer time,

15
00:01:16,194 --> 00:01:17,700
without live traffic.

16
00:01:18,150 --> 00:01:24,386
Analytics combines fresh GPS with recent, unique crowd reports. Configurable thresholds determine

17
00:01:24,386 --> 00:01:30,621
crowding. Sustained high crowding for ten minutes creates an alert; stale or

18
00:01:30,621 --> 00:01:32,700
insufficient evidence resets continuity.

19
00:01:33,150 --> 00:01:39,172
Operator and GPS endpoints use separate roles. Dispatch validates the line, full

20
00:01:39,172 --> 00:01:45,194
trajectory, and reserve bus. A transaction protects assignment, saves history, and starts

21
00:01:45,194 --> 00:01:46,700
the simulated vehicle.

22
00:01:47,150 --> 00:01:53,174
Unit, integration, and browser tests are included, although the latest full suite

23
00:01:53,174 --> 00:01:59,198
was not rerun. Real GPS, schedules, and calibrated arrival estimates are future

24
00:01:59,198 --> 00:01:59,700
integrations.
